Feature: tools/gen-ucum-table.py writes src/ucum_table.generated.rs, and checks it
  The script is not crate code and the functional suite in tests/ never
  runs it, so these scenarios load it in-process. `make script-tests` runs
  them under coverage for SonarQube Cloud. Each works on a copy of the
  committed table in target/script-tests/.

  Scenario: The header names the generator, its source and the date
    When the table is rendered on "2000-01-02"
    Then its first line is "// @generated by tools/gen-ucum-table.py on 2000-01-02."
    And its second line names vendor/ucum-essence.xml in the ucum-units repository
    And its fourth line says to run make ucum-table

  Scenario: The committed table is current
    Given a copy of the committed table
    When the script runs with "--check"
    Then it prints "ucum-table: current"

  Scenario: The check ignores only the date
    Given a copy of the committed table stamped "2000-01-02"
    When the script runs with "--check"
    Then it prints "current"

  Scenario: The check fails on a stale table
    Given a copy of the committed table with "lm" changed to "xx"
    When the script runs with "--check"
    Then it stops, saying "is stale: run `make ucum-table`"

  Scenario: An unchanged table keeps its date
    Given a copy of the committed table stamped "2000-01-02"
    When the script runs
    Then the table is still stamped "2000-01-02"
    And it prints "current"

  Scenario: A changed table takes today's date
    Given a copy of the committed table stamped "2000-01-02" with "lm" changed to "xx"
    When the script runs
    Then the table is the committed one stamped today
    And it prints "wrote target/script-tests/ucum_table.generated.rs"

  Scenario: A missing table is written with today's date
    Given a copy of the committed table
    And the copy is removed
    When the script runs
    Then the table is the committed one stamped today
